{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thread pool starvation avoidance thread pool starvation avoidance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","fileName":"Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thread pool starvation avoidance thread pool starvation avoidance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","fileName":"Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance","heading":"Thread Pool Starvation Avoidance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Thread-pool starvation occurs when queued work cannot obtain workers because existing workers remain occupied, often by blocking waits. A runtime can detect inadequate progress and inject additional threads so the queue does not remain stalled.\n\nInjection is a recovery mechanism with ramp-up time and resource cost, not permission to block without limit. Asynchronous I/O and bounded concurrency address the workload cause more directly by returning workers while operations wait.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore